A||||4||BAM-BAM||Power mirrors, HELP?||||11||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-14-2000||11:12 PM||||  Hey guys, heres the problem. Power mirrors are out of commision and I want them to work.<BR>When I first got the car they worked a little bit, but they have long sense ceased to function <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. I was wondering if anyone has ever had to deal with the power mirrors before. Is it probable that I need to replace the switch, or, is the mirror motor usually the culprit. How would I test the switch / motor? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Any input is helpful.<P>  Thanx, BAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Phil||03-15-2000||06:32 AM||||If both mirrors don't work I would suspect the wiring/switch, if it's only one could be the motor or the piviots in the mirror||||reg||1
Z||000002||Earne||03-15-2000||06:53 AM||||Phil nailed it BAM-BAM.  Both mirrors are likely to be the rocker switch.  The contacts corrode over time.  You could try removing it, spraying it with contact cleaner and exercising it.  That worked for me for a while, then I gave up and bought a new one.  They are still available at the dealer and from the Fireo Store.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||03-16-2000||08:31 PM||||   Thanks alot guys. As usual,, you are heading me in the right direction, I know it.<BR>I will take a look at it this weekend. Thanks again.<BR>  <P> Bam Out!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
